# ${SRC_DIR}/tests/

Tests for ${PROJECT_NAME}.

## Layout

- [`unit/`](unit/) — pure function tests. Mock everything I/O.
- [`integration/`](integration/) — wire one feature end-to-end (route → controller → service). Use `supertest`.
- [`fixtures/`](fixtures/) — sample payloads and request bodies.

## What lives here

- `*.spec.ts` / `*.test.ts` files. Jest discovers both suffixes via the root `jest.config.ts`.
- One folder per category — never mix unit and integration in the same folder.

## What does NOT live here

- Tests that exercise live external services. Those belong in a separate
  `tests/e2e/` folder (not part of the default `npm test` run).

## Naming

- `<feature>.spec.ts` — unit test for `<feature>'s` service.
- `<feature>.integration.spec.ts` — integration test for the feature's route.

## A baseline test

[`unit/health.spec.ts`](unit/health.spec.ts) covers the example `health`
feature. Keep similar coverage as you add features.

